WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.053
JAMIE: True. It's built for
professional work — visual

00:00:03.053 --> 00:00:06.107
JAMIE: understanding, automated
computer tasks — not the hardest

00:00:06.107 --> 00:00:09.160
JAMIE: reasoning problems. But
honestly? Most real-world tasks
aren't

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.213
JAMIE: the hardest reasoning
problems.

00:00:12.393 --> 00:00:14.530
ALEX: Rufus, take us on location.

00:00:16.522 --> 00:00:19.339
RUFUS: Picture the trading floor.
Not the cinematic one

00:00:19.339 --> 00:00:22.157
RUFUS: — the real one, quieter,
mostly monitors. When

00:00:22.157 --> 00:00:24.974
RUFUS: OpenAI announced Terra on
October twenty-sixth, the number

00:00:24.974 --> 00:00:27.791
RUFUS: that landed with
infrastructure buyers wasn't the
benchmark.

00:00:27.791 --> 00:00:30.609
RUFUS: It was fifty percent.
Because the pricing cut

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:33.426
RUFUS: is what matters most here —
